      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some typical regimens. Tell me which one you want, or give me a different dose:\n\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day) for mild to moderate pain or fever\n- **600 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is the usual regimen for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the absolute ceiling and is generally used only under close supervision\n\nDid you mean 400 mg, or 1600 mg total per day? If you do want the original dose, please confirm that it's intentional and give me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to review it."
      }
     ],
